1. ENVIRONMENT SETUP

Before running the project, create a .env file in the root folder and add the
following keys. Follow the setup instructions below for each one.


SETTING UP MONGODB

Option 1: Local MongoDB

  1. Download and install MongoDB Community Edition from:
     https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/community

  2. Start the MongoDB service:
       Windows : MongoDB runs as a service automatically after install
       Mac     : brew services start mongodb-community
       Linux   : sudo systemctl start mongod

  3. Add this to your .env file:
     MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/foresightwallet


Option 2: MongoDB Atlas (Cloud - Free)

  1. Go to https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas and create a free account
  2. Create a new free cluster (M0 tier)
  3. When prompted, create a database user and save the username and password
  4. Under Network Access, click Add IP Address and select Allow Access from Anywhere
  5. Go to Database, click Connect, and choose Drivers
  6. Copy the connection string which looks like:
     mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/
  7. Replace username and password with your database user credentials
  8. Add this to your .env file:
     MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://youruser:yourpassword@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/foresightwallet


SETTING UP SECRET KEY

Flask uses this to sign and encrypt session cookies to keep users logged in
securely. Add any random string to your .env file:

  SECRET_KEY=foresightwallet2026


SETTING UP GEMINI API KEY

The WalletWise AI chatbot uses Google's Gemini API (gemini-2.5-flash-lite model).

  1. Go to https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
  2. Sign in with a Google account
  3. Click Create API Key
  4. Copy the key and add it to your .env file:
     GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key_here

Note: The free tier of Google AI Studio is sufficient to run this project.


SETTING UP GOOGLE OAUTH

Google OAuth allows users to sign in with their Google account.

  1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and sign in
  2. Create a new project or select an existing one
  3. In the left menu go to APIs & Services, then OAuth consent screen
       - Select External and click Create
       - Fill in the app name (e.g. Foresight Wallet) and your email
       - Click Save and Continue through the remaining steps
  4. Go to APIs & Services, then Credentials
  5. Click Create Credentials and select OAuth 2.0 Client ID
  6. Set Application type to Web application
  7. Under Authorised redirect URIs add:
     http://localhost:5000/google/callback
  8. Click Create, you will receive a Client ID and Client Secret
  9. Add both to your .env file:
     GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
     GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret_here


2. INSTALLATION

  1. Extract the submitted ZIP file ForesightWallet_Tahmid_Islam_220005783.zip 
     Open the extracted ForesightWallet-main
     folder in VS Code, then open a terminal inside VS Code using:
     Terminal menu → New Terminal

  2. Create a virtual environment:
       Windows  : py -m venv venv
       Mac/Linux: python3 -m venv venv

  3. Activate the virtual environment:
       Windows  : First run: Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
                  Then run:  venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
       Mac/Linux: source venv/bin/activate

  4. Install dependencies:
     pip install -r requirements.txt

  5. Create a .env file in the root folder with all keys from Section 1:

     MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_uri
     SECRET_KEY=your_secret_key
     GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key
     GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id
     GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret

  6. Run the application:
     python app.py or py app.py

  7. Open your browser and go to:
     http://127.0.0.1:5000

To run the application again after initial setup:

     venv\Scripts\activate
     python app.py or py app.py

Then open http://127.0.0.1:5000



3. FOLDER STRUCTURE

ForesightWallet/
├── app.py                          # Flask app factory, registers all blueprints
├── extensions.py                   # MongoDB collections (spending, budget, users)
├── helpers.py                      # Shared utility functions and calculate_month_summary
├── Procfile                        # gunicorn app:app (Render deployment)
├── runtime.txt                     # python-3.10.13
├── requirements.txt                # Python dependencies
├── .gitignore                      # Files excluded from version control
├── .gitattributes                  # Git line ending and diff settings
├── budgetwise_finance_dataset.csv  # Synthetic dataset used to train ML models
├── routes/
│   ├── auth.py                     # Register, login, Google OAuth, logout
│   ├── budget.py                   # Budget tracker + /api/prev-month-balance
│   ├── dashboard.py                # Main dashboard
│   ├── spending.py                 # Spending log CRUD
│   ├── feedback.py                 # Personalised feedback (rule-based)
│   ├── income_trends.py            # Income trends charts
│   ├── spending_trends.py          # Spending trends charts
│   ├── planned_deductions.py       # Planned deductions history
│   ├── prediction.py               # Spending forecast (Random Forest)
│   ├── category_prediction.py      # Top category prediction
│   ├── clustering.py               # K-Means spending behaviour clustering
│   ├── risk.py                     # Financial risk indicator
│   └── walletwise.py               # WalletWise AI chatbot (Gemini API)
├── ml_models/
│   ├── spending_forecast_model.pkl # Random Forest forecast model
│   ├── forecast_feature_cols.pkl   # Feature columns for forecast model
│   ├── kmeans_model.pkl            # K-Means clustering model
│   ├── kmeans_scaler.pkl           # Scaler for K-Means
│   ├── kmeans_feature_cols.pkl     # Feature columns for K-Means
│   └── kmeans_cluster_labels.pkl   # Cluster label mappings
├── ml_training/
│   ├── train_spending_forecast_model.py  # Trained the Random Forest model on the synthetic dataset and saved the .pkl files to ml_models
│   └── train_kmeans_model.py             # Trained the K-Means clustering model and saved the .pkl files to ml_models
├── static/
│   ├── LogoN.png                   # App logo
│   ├── style.css                   # All styles consolidated
│   └── js/
│       ├── sidebar.js              # Sidebar toggle (desktop + mobile)
│       ├── base.js                 # Dark mode + WalletWise chat
│       ├── budget_tracker.js       # Progress bar, edit toggle, carry forward
│       ├── dashboard.js            # KPI cards, donut charts, bar chart
│       ├── income_trends.js        # Income trends charts
│       ├── planned_deductions.js   # Planned deductions charts
│       ├── prediction.js           # Feature switcher
│       ├── prediction_forecast.js  # Forecast chart
│       ├── spending_log.js         # Spending log interactions
│       └── spending_trends.js      # Spending trends charts
└── templates/
    ├── base.html                   # Sidebar, navbar, dark mode
    ├── dashboard.html              # Main dashboard
    ├── budget_tracker.html         # Budget tracker
    ├── spending_log.html           # Spending log
    ├── income_trends.html          # Income trends
    ├── spending_trends.html        # Spending trends
    ├── planned_deductions.html     # Planned deductions
    ├── prediction.html             # Forecast + category + clustering
    ├── feedback.html               # Personalised feedback
    ├── risk.html                   # Financial risk indicator
    ├── landing.html                # Landing page
    ├── login.html                  # Login page
    └── register.html               # Register page



4. TECH STACK

  Backend        : Python 3.10, Flask 3.0.2
  Templating     : Jinja2
  Database       : MongoDB (PyMongo 4.16.0)
  Frontend       : HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Bootstrap 5.3.2
  Charts         : ApexCharts 3.44.0
  ML Models      : scikit-learn 1.8.0, joblib 1.3.2
  AI Chatbot     : Google Gemini API (gemini-2.5-flash-lite)
  Authentication : Google OAuth 2.0, Flask-Bcrypt
  Deployment     : Render (gunicorn 21.2.0)
  PDF Export     : jsPDF, html2canvas


5. FEATURE OVERVIEW

  Dashboard                  : KPI cards showing starting balance, end balance,
                               net effect, projected balance, daily burn rate
                               and budget usage for any selected month

  Spending Log               : Add, edit and delete income and expense
                               transactions by category and date

  Budget Tracker             : Set monthly spending limits, account balance and
                               income. Tracks progress with a visual meter and
                               alerts when nearing the limit

  Spending Trends            : Interactive daily and monthly spending charts
                               with period comparison and PDF export

  Income Trends              : Monthly income charts with year overview and
                               PDF export

  Planned Deductions         : Track recurring savings, bills and debt payments
                               over time with breakdown charts

  Personalised Feedback      : Rule-based spending tips generated from actual
                               transaction categories each month

  ML Spending Forecast       : Random Forest model predicts whether you will
                               exceed your budget in the next 30 days

  Top Category Prediction    : Predicts which spending category will be highest
                               next month

  Spending Behaviour         : K-Means model classifies spending behaviour
  Clustering                   as Saver, Balanced or Leisure-Heavy

  Financial Risk Indicator   : Colour-coded risk score out of 100 based on
                               spending, income and savings behaviour

  WalletWise AI Chatbot      : Gemini-powered assistant that answers finance
                               questions and looks up live prices

  Dark Mode                  : Full dark/light mode toggle across all pages

  Google OAuth               : Sign in with Google in addition to standard
                               email and password registration

  PDF Export                 : Download charts as PDF files from spending
                               trends, income trends, planned deductions and
                               prediction pages


